  "result": "I found the bug and wrote a fix plan. I haven't edited any code yet because plan mode is on. I couldn't send the plan for approval because the approval tool (ExitPlanMode) isn't available in this session, so I'm laying it out here instead.\n\n**Cause:** In `src/click/core.py:386-392`, a subcommand inherits the parent's entire `default_map` instead of just the entry under its own name. With `default_map={\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}`, the `runserver` subcommand looks for `port` at the top level of the map. It doesn't find it there, so the configured default is ignored.\n\n**Fix:** a one-line change at `src/click/core.py:392`:\n```python\ndefault_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)\n```\nThe check just above it already makes sure neither `info_name` nor the parent's map is `None`.\n\n**Tests:** add regression tests in `tests/test_defaults.py` for:\n- a group with one subcommand, where `default_map={\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}` should give a port of 5000;\n- groups nested two levels deep.\n\n**Check:** run `pytest tests/` and the example in `docs/commands.md`.\n\nThe full plan is in `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-mighty-axolotl.md`. Tell me to go ahead and I'll make the change.",
